<title>UK: Toyota prices $1.0 bln five-year bond.</title>
<headline>Toyota prices $1.0 bln five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier in Tokyo by joint lead managers Credit Suisse First Boston and Merrill Lynch, has been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TOYOTA MOTOR CORP</p>
<p> AMT    $1.0 BLN	COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    22.JUL.02</p>
<p> TYPE   EURO-ASIAN    ISS PRICE  101.175   PAY DATE    22.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.55     SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LON/HK/SI PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100</p>
<p>SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/HK/SI</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  JAPAN     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT JUNE 2002 U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
